A||N||9||jhogans||Detailing Products?||||5||
Z||000000||jhogans||12-07-1999||07:55 PM||||What does everybody use for detailing their cars as far as:<BR>Car Wash<BR>Wax<BR>Wheel Cleaners<BR>Rim Cleaners<BR>Engine Cleaners<BR>Window Cleaners<BR>Vinyle/leather Cleaners<BR>etc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||12-07-1999||08:19 PM||||I use my son <p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 12-07-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||12-07-1999||08:31 PM||||Good one Phil! "Wax on, wax off"! I vary on most products, except wax. Turtle wax emerald series is the best I've ever used.||||reg||12
Z||000003||Cooter||12-07-1999||09:33 PM||||Turtle wax car wash soap and what ever I have laying around for wax. Usually use Meguire's polishes and buffing products. I just waxed my DuckMobile with Prolong's one step sealant/wax. It went on really easy and feels slick.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-07-1999||09:49 PM||||I use meguiars wax, turtle wax car wash, and armor all products for my wheels, tires, and interior. I know, I've heard what people say about Armor All interior spray, it's never happened to me, so I just disreguard it. Meguires outside(excpet tires and wheels), armor all inside. Eagle One is another very good brand I use. Windows, I use Armor all window cleaner, engine cleaner is WD-40.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-08-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-07-1999||11:31 PM||||fiero56--I've owned and shown a couple of VERY nice trucks (18 wheelers) and I can tell you that Armor All WILL dry out and crack your dash eventually.  Besides, it stays greasy which attracts dirt.  STPs product has moisturizers in it to keep it from drying out the dash, but it's still greasy.  There is actually an interior wax that I have used in shows and it looks good.  I forget the name as I've been out of the truck for a few months (thank, God!).  I'll look for it in the garage tomorrow.  Try windex on the dash, doors, etc.  It works well, although it has to be repeated more often than the petroleum based "cleaners".  And it won't collect dust and dirt.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||12-08-1999||08:42 AM||||I've heard that they also make a "grease free" formula, comes in a black bottle. Would it be better for the dash and other materials?<BR>I haven't had a chance to try that stuff yet.  I only use Armor All maybe twice a year, If that much, so one bottle lasts forever. <BR>I would like to know more about this interior wax. I've only cleaned my Fiero once(with armor all), and might consder switching to another product. I chose to use armor all since I've heard "they're all the same". Sprays that is, stp, son of a gun, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Scott2M4||12-08-1999||09:56 AM||||Armor All for rubber, plastic and vinyl.  Meguires #2, #9 and #26 for paint.  Windex for windows.<P>Here's a little trick I learned while in the detailing business:  use newspaper on the windows instead of a towel.  Streak-free every time.  Downside is dirty hands and be careful when using it on the interior around light-colored cloth.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Voyd||12-08-1999||01:51 PM||||when i bought my car at first it was all cruddy with dirt makrs everywhere. to thoroughly clean it i used a product called Vim. its a white creme cleanser with bleach in it, but its not an abrasive. it works AWESOME on the dash and door areas. once u clean it with this, youll never need to do it again if youre a clean person. subsequent cleaning only use a bit of Armor All and it works fine.<P>outside its just good old soap n water, and good scrubbin. once in a while break out the Turtle Wax creme and it works great.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Voyd (edited 12-08-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-08-1999||01:53 PM||||There is nothing petroleum based that will be 100% grease free.  I still say that you should never use Armor All, not even on the tires.  It will dry everything out.  Still looking for that interior wax. All the cleaners aren't the same.  They are all similar, though.  All of the petroleum based ones will be greasy and attract dirt/dust.  You might not notice it too much in a car that doesn't get driven much, but it's terrible in a truck (150,000miles/year).  If you use Armor All, etc. and drive much (especially in the summer with your windows down), you will notice that you not only get dirt/dust, but clumps of it.  But everyone's entitled to their opinion.  That's what makes this forum so great.||||reg||1
